# Supabase project credentials.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values from your Supabase project
# (Project Settings > API). Never commit the real .env file.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# SERVER-ONLY Supabase service-role key (Project Settings > API). Used by the
# GREENLINE community-track publish endpoint (/api/greenline-track-publish),
# which must validate submitted tracks in Node before writing — there is no
# client write path to greenline_tracks. Read at runtime via
# $env/dynamic/private, so leaving it blank is safe: publishing responds
# "not configured" and everything else works. NEVER expose this to the client
# and never prefix it PUBLIC_. Set it in the Vercel project env for production.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# RETIRED, August 2026: COIN_API_KEY and COIN_LEDGER_URL. They configured the
# Google Sheets / Apps Script coin ledger, which is retired -- the IDEA Coin
# economy lives entirely in Supabase now. Both variables should be REMOVED from
# the Vercel project env; nothing reads them. See
# docs/coin-economy/archive/legacy-system/README.md for what they did.

# FSP tech-selection Apps Script endpoint (the /fsp-tech-selection tool posts
# freshman rankings here, and prefills via GET ?email=). Deploy the Google
# Apps Script web app, then paste its /exec URL here. Read at runtime via
# $env/dynamic/public, so leaving it blank is safe: the page loads and the
# picker works, it just shows "saving is not configured yet" instead of posting.
# PLACEHOLDER — replace with the real deployed /exec URL.
PUBLIC_FSP_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=

# Web Push (tournament match alerts). Generate a pair once with:
#   node -e "const wp=require('web-push');console.log(wp.generateVAPIDKeys())"
# The PUBLIC key identifies this server to browser push services and is safe
# in the client bundle (read at runtime via $env/dynamic/public, so a missing
# value degrades to "alerts unavailable", never a build break). The PRIVATE
# key signs every push send and is SERVER-ONLY ($env/dynamic/private): NEVER
# prefix it PUBLIC_, never commit it. Both keys must come from the SAME pair
# or every send is rejected. Set both in the Vercel project env. Subscriptions
# are minted against the public key, so changing the pair orphans existing
# subscriptions (they fail silently and users re-enable).
PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Optional VAPID contact (mailto: or https: URL) sent to push services with
# each push; defaults to https://ideabosco.com in src/lib/server/push.ts.
VAPID_SUBJECT=

# FSP Pulse Check Apps Script endpoint (the /fsp-pulse tool posts FRC interest
# + pathway pulse rankings here, and prefills via GET ?email=). Deploy the
# Google Apps Script web app, then paste its /exec URL here. Read at runtime
# via $env/dynamic/public, so leaving it blank is safe: the page loads and the
# picker works, it just shows "saving is not configured yet" instead of posting.
# PLACEHOLDER — replace with the real deployed /exec URL.
PUBLIC_FSP_PULSE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=

# SERVER-ONLY digital-notebook Drive integration (src/lib/server/notebook-drive.ts,
# the only module that reads these). Photo uploads from /api/notebook/upload and
# /api/notebook/add-photo land in a folder inside a Google SHARED DRIVE;
# Postgres stores only the Drive file id (migration 0069).
#
# Auth is OAUTH ON BEHALF OF A REAL BOSCO TECH ACCOUNT, not a service account:
# the shared drive blocks any identity outside the school's Workspace domain,
# so a service account can never be granted access. Setup:
#   1. In Google Cloud, enable the Drive API and create an OAuth client
#      (type "Web application") whose authorized redirect URI is EXACTLY
#      https://ideabosco.com/admin/drive-connect/callback
#   2. Set GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET in the Vercel
#      project env and redeploy.
#   3. As a site ADMIN (0067), visit https://ideabosco.com/admin/drive-connect
#      once and approve access, signed in as a school account that can write
#      to the notebook folder in the shared drive. The consent asks for the
#      FULL https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive scope (not drive.file: the
#      target folder pre-exists in the shared drive, and drive.file cannot
#      reliably create files inside a folder the app neither created nor was
#      granted through a Picker flow). The callback displays a
#      refresh token EXACTLY ONCE (never logged, never stored server-side).
#   4. Copy it into the Vercel project env as GOOGLE_DRIVE_REFRESH_TOKEN and
#      redeploy. Uploads work from the next deploy.
# All three are read at runtime via $env/dynamic/private, so leaving them blank
# is safe: the two notebook upload routes answer 503 "not configured" and
# nothing else is affected. NEVER prefix any of them with PUBLIC_.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Optional override for the notebook photo folder (a folder INSIDE the shared
# drive, not a shared-drive root). The current folder id is the default in
# src/lib/server/notebook-drive.ts -- the literal in the code is the working
# value and this var is only the override -- so it only needs setting if the
# folder ever moves.
GOOGLE_DRIVE_NOTEBOOK_FOLDER_ID=

# GitHub export for classroom specs (0110). A FINE-GRAINED personal access
# token scoped to Contents: read and write on pina-hash/idea-app AND NOTHING
# ELSE -- it exists to commit one folder of JSON under materials/, so a classic
# token or a broader scope is more access than the feature can use.
#
# Read at runtime via $env/dynamic/private by src/lib/server/classroom-export.ts
# and by nothing else, so leaving it BLANK is safe and is the normal state for
# local development: the export is skipped silently, no failure is recorded, and
# no chip appears anywhere. Set it in the Vercel project env for production.
# NEVER expose it to the client and never prefix it PUBLIC_.
GITHUB_EXPORT_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDEA FOUNDRY BUNDLES.
#
# NOTHING SUPABASE-HOSTED SERVES A BUNDLE ANY MORE, and the reason is measured
# rather than assumed. Two independent Supabase subsystems refuse to emit HTML:
# Storage's renderer rewrites `text/html` to `text/plain` on the public, the
# authenticated and the signed-URL paths alike, and the hosted Edge Function
# gateway does the SAME rewrite and additionally replaces the function's own
# CSP with `default-src 'none'; sandbox`, which blanks the page even once the
# type is corrected. Different codebases, same refusal: it is a platform
# posture against serving arbitrary HTML off `*.supabase.co`, not a bug. So the
# bytes come off a host whose headers we set.
#
# WHAT SERVES A BUNDLE NOW is an ordinary SvelteKit route on this same Vercel
# project:
#
#   <apps origin>/b/<app id>/<version id>/
#
# built by `src/lib/foundry/bundle-url.ts` and answered by
# `src/routes/b/[appId]/[versionId]/[...path]/+server.ts`. There is no token, no
# mint, no `hooks.server.ts` host branch and no build step that rewrites the
# route table -- those three are what the deleted proxy failed on, and none of
# them exists here.

# The origin bundles are served from: a SECOND DOMAIN on this same Vercel
# project. Read at runtime via $env/dynamic/public.
#
# WHY A SECOND ORIGIN AND NOT A PATH ON THE MAIN HOST. The portal's session
# cookies are set by @supabase/ssr with NO Domain attribute, so they are
# HOST-ONLY on ideabosco.com and are never sent to apps.ideabosco.com. A bundle
# containing <img src="/api/whatever"> therefore reaches a host that holds no
# session, because there is no cookie there to send -- an ABSENCE, not a
# browser declining to send one. That is the whole reason for the split.
#
# LEAVING IT BLANK REMOVES THE LAUNCH CONTROL EVERYWHERE, deliberately. The
# alternative -- falling back to the current origin -- would serve student
# bundles off the main, cookie-carrying host, silently, on any deployment that
# forgot this. A missing launch button is a bug report on the first day.
PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_APPS_ORIGIN=

# The portal's own origin, which becomes the bundle response's CSP
# `frame-ancestors` so only ideabosco.com may embed a published app. Read at
# runtime via $env/dynamic/public.
#
# UNSET MEANS UNRESTRICTED, which reverses the deleted proxy's rule on purpose.
# On a feature whose history is silently serving nothing, a variable whose
# absence blanks every frame is the worse failure -- and a framed bundle is
# sandboxed, holds no session and can reach nothing of ours, so another site
# embedding one gains a copy of a student's app and no more than that.
PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_PORTAL_ORIGIN=

# RETIRED, and to be DELETED from the Vercel project: PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_APPS_HOST,
# PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_APP_ORIGIN and FOUNDRY_TOKEN_SECRET (the token proxy), plus
# COIN_API_KEY and COIN_LEDGER_URL (the Sheets coin ledger). Nothing reads any
# of them. The Supabase function secret FOUNDRY_APP_ORIGIN is retired too --
# `supabase secrets unset FOUNDRY_APP_ORIGIN` -- and it never took effect
# anyway, because the gateway was replacing that CSP wholesale.
#
# What isolates a bundle is the iframe sandbox with no `allow-same-origin`,
# which puts the document in an opaque origin, plus the same flags sent as a
# CSP `sandbox` directive so a direct navigation lands in the same place, plus
# the bytes coming off the apps origin rather than off ideabosco.com -- so a
# request a bundle makes carries no cookie of the portal's, because there are
# none on that origin to carry.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PORTED HTML ASSIGNMENTS (the /hx serving route).
#
# A ported HTML assignment is a single document a student's work happens
# inside, served by `src/routes/hx/[docId]/` under a CSP that carries
# `sandbox allow-scripts`, `connect-src 'none'` and `form-action 'none'` -- so
# an uploaded document runs in an opaque origin and cannot exfiltrate what is
# typed into it. The two variables below decide WHERE it is served from and WHO
# may frame it. Both are read at runtime via $env/dynamic/public.
#
# THE `sandbox` DIRECTIVE IS WHY NEITHER VARIABLE IS LOAD-BEARING FOR SAFETY
# ANY MORE. It was added after the route shipped without one: the iframe's own
# `sandbox` attribute governs a document the portal FRAMED, so a student who
# typed or pasted a `/hx/` URL reached the same bytes with no frame around them
# and therefore no attribute. With PUBLIC_HX_SANDBOX_ORIGIN unset the route
# answers on ideabosco.com, where the session cookies live and where
# @supabase/ssr writes them httpOnly: false, so `document.cookie` can read
# them. The directive closes that, and it is sent whatever these two say.

# The origin ported documents are served from: a SEPARATE DOMAIN on this same
# Vercel project, the way PUBLIC_FOUNDRY_APPS_ORIGIN is for bundles, and for
# the same reason -- the portal's session cookies are set by @supabase/ssr with
# no Domain attribute, so they are HOST-ONLY on ideabosco.com and simply do not
# exist on the document host. That absence is what the split buys; no header
# achieves it.
#
# SET IT ON PRODUCTION ONLY (https://sandbox.ideabosco.com, once that domain
# and its DNS record exist on the Vercel project). UNSET, the route answers on
# ANY host, which is correct for local development and for a Vercel preview:
# a preview deploys to exactly one host, so one server is answering both the
# portal role and the document role and there is no second origin to name.
#
# IT IS DEFENCE IN DEPTH NOW, NOT A PREREQUISITE, AND IT IS STILL THE STRONGER
# DEPLOYMENT. Before the CSP carried a `sandbox` directive, leaving this unset
# in production meant an uploaded document could be navigated to directly on
# the cookie-carrying host. That is closed at the browser now. What a second
# host still buys is an ABSENCE rather than a browser honouring a directive:
# the cookies are not merely unreadable there, they are not there. An absence
# cannot regress, so set it in production even though production is safe
# without it.
PUBLIC_HX_SANDBOX_ORIGIN=

# The portal origin that becomes the document response's CSP `frame-ancestors`,
# so only the portal may embed a ported document. Resolved rather than read, in
# `src/routes/hx/_headers.ts` (which arrives with the route): this variable when
# set, otherwise https://ideabosco.com but ONLY when PUBLIC_HX_SANDBOX_ORIGIN is
# itself set, otherwise the origin the request arrived on. So production -- the
# sandbox origin set, this one left blank -- reproduces the contract's literal
# policy byte for byte without anybody typing it.
#
# LEAVE IT UNSET ON A PREVIEW, AND LEAVE PUBLIC_HX_SANDBOX_ORIGIN UNSET WITH
# IT. Naming an origin here on a preview makes `frame-ancestors` name a host
# that is not framing anything -- the preview's own host is doing the framing --
# and the browser then refuses to let the harness embed a document at all, which
# reads as a broken feature rather than as a misconfiguration. The same is true
# one rung up: setting PUBLIC_HX_SANDBOX_ORIGIN alone on a preview resolves
# `frame-ancestors` to https://ideabosco.com, which is not that preview either.
# Both unset is the configuration that works everywhere but production, and
# production is the one deployment where the two roles are genuinely two hosts.
PUBLIC_HX_PORTAL_ORIGIN=
